"file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "16a0ebc5e06e1189ea7fe5612c5a4a2fd3b0947108223d014dd9157cbea4d864" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4(-2) & =0 \\\\ 5-\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "16a0ebc5e06e1189ea7fe5612c5a4a2fd3b0947108223d014dd9157cbea4d864" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224