n" "q-103537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{5}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "16a0ebc5e06e1189ea7fe5612c5a4a2fd3b0947108223d014dd9157cbea4d864" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "16a0ebc5e06e1189ea7fe5612c5a4a2fd3b0947108223d014dd9157cbea4d864" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/example-5904.json" "file_sha256" "37d058f18c0b9489cc1836a4403b5c583fe27233aa019ab47207bd008c98153d" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2(-2) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(5)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/example-5904.json" "file_sha256" "37d058f18c0b9489cc1836a4403b5c583fe27233aa019ab47207bd008c98153d" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ and $\\lambda_2$ are eigenvalues of a real $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find $2(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/example-5905.json" "file_sha256" "cf60857ece178b1d41dba6cdaa03e05ba7f12f6d3c18b3af65eeb84f2178b74c" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda_1.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\lambda_2=\\overline{\\lambda}_1=-2-3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =2(-2+3\\text{i}+(-2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(-4) \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/example-5905.json" "file_sha256" "cf60857ece178b1d41dba6cdaa03e05ba7f12f6d3c18b3af65eeb84f2178b74c" "basis" 1439 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-81145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 13 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 13 \\\\ -1 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 13 \\\\ -1 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-13(-1) & =0 \\\\ -5-5\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+13 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(8)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-81145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-4\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =4\\pm 4\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4(-2) & =0 \\\\ 5-\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =-2\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-3\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =3\\pm 3\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_c