hacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-102774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm \\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -17 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -17 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -17 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-1(-17) & =0 \\\\ -1-\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+17 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =4\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-1(-2) & =0 \\\\ -1-\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-81020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =-1\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5+4\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $\\frac{2}{5}({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5+4\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=-5-4\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =\\frac{2}{5}((-5+4\\text{i})+(-5-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(-10) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{5}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{5}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-103537" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=5+3\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $\\frac{2}{3}({\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=5+3\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=5-3\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}({\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}) & =\\frac{2}{3}(5+3\\text{i}-(5-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(6\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-102775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "2\\text{i}"] ["math" "4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-102775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=6-\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $3({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=6-\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=6+\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =3(6-\\text{i}+(6+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(12) \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :quest