complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=5+6\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}({\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{4}(5-6\\text{i}-(5+6\\text{i})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-12\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-81034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\text{i}"] ["math" "-6\\text{i}"] ["math" "3\\text{i}"] ["math" "4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-81034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+2\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $2({\\lambda }_{2}-{\\lambda }_{1}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+2\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=4-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }_{2}-{\\lambda }_{1}) & =2(4-2\\text{i}-(4+2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(-4\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e457a3133ac960b144762b16026b7c779655cccc1986c6f9a1759a89cfe2a206"} {"question" "q-39184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-8\\text{i}"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "16-8\\text{i}"] ["math" "8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "q-39184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad21d172321c7557e13759311e14dc2468f8b02ebbf6cd9c920271bdf3a7570"} {"question" "e-5904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/assets/61d1e4670c482f79d4b87ff36bb772339a704df18ccfb624ce183729f5022c4c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/example-5904.json" "file_sha256" "80deaa861a2eb307ca254e74b372d9a835df3601a1a8956f04de43bfac767f4f"} {"question" "e-5904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/assets/8bfd617b360f6bed1fcf835ebe52c56f3c7b6a5a5234e099f7a0aec0d4bbdc36.png)\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2(-2) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(5)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/example-5904.json" "file_sha256" "80deaa861a2eb307ca254e74b372d9a835df3601a1a8956f04de43bfac767f4f"} {"question" "e-5905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ and $\\lambda_2$ are eigenvalues of a real $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find $2(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/example-5905.json" "file_sha256" "9b06e5bc2636625a2c58a83a5682eaa58653eada078d918ecd60fa151f08af46"} {"question" "e-5905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda_1.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\lambda_2=\\overline{\\lambda}_1=-2-3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =2(-2+3\\text{i}+(-2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(-4) \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069899/example-5905.json" "file_sha256" "9b06e5bc2636625a2c58a83a5682eaa58653eada078d918ecd60fa151f08af46"}] "usage" {"q-39186" [] "q-103537" [] "q-81144" [] "e-5905" [] "e-5904" [] "q-102775" [] "q-39184" [] "q-81036" []} "basis" 2412 "retractions" [[17592186129659 :question/problem "Given that $λ_{1} = 4 + 2\\textrm{i}$ and $λ_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix $A$, find $2(λ_{2} - λ_{1})$."] [17592186128911 :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186128911 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2(-2) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(5)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186127749 17592186127750 17592186127751 17592186127752 17592186127753 17592186307629 17592186307630 17592186307631 17592186307632 17592186307633 17592186307643 17592186307644 17592186307645 17592186307646 17592186307647 17592186307650 17592186307651 17592186307652 17592186307653 17592186307654 17592186307678 17592186307679 17592186307680 17592186307681 17592186307682 17592186307685 17592186307686 17592186307687 17592186307688 17592186307689] "immutable_fields" [[17592186127748 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127748 :answer-field/id] [17592186127748 :answer-field/key] [17592186127748 :answer-field/type] [17592186307628 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307628 :answer-field/id] [17592186307628 :answer-field/key] [17592186307628 :answer-field/type] [17592186307642 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307642 :answer-field/id] [17592186307642 :answer-field/key] [17592186307642 :answer-field/type] [17592186307649 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307649 :answer-field/id] [17592186307649 :answer-field/key] [17592186307649 :answer-field/type] [17592186307677 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307677 :answer-field/id] [17